<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lviv</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Lemberg, Lwów</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lviv is the largest city of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, founded in the mid-13th century by King Daniel of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galicia">Galicia</a> and named after his son Leo. It passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> in 1349, was the capital of the Austrian crownland of Galicia as Lemberg from 1772 to 1918 and then belonged to Poland until 1939. Its historic centre is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p></div>
